CHAPTER.VERS:
Men: brothers and fathers, hear

          {+}
         the defense which I now make to you

          {+}
        .

I am a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but brought up in this city, instructed at the feet of Gamaliel according to the strict manner of the law of our fathers, being zealous for God even as all of you

          {+}
         are this day:

And when they had tied him up with the thongs, Paul said to the captain that stood by, Is it lawful for you

          {+}
         to scourge a man who is a Roman, and uncondemned?
